# Markdown math

The Markdown preview in this repo does not render LaTeX. In every `.md` file, write equations and formulas as Unicode symbols, using `formulas/Chapter4-VectorSpaces.md` as the model.

- Put a display equation on its own line and bold it: `**𝐮 + 𝐯 = (u₁ + v₁, …, uₙ + vₙ)**`
- Use symbols in tables and sentences the same way: `𝐯 ∈ V`, `W ⊆ V`, `ℝⁿ`, `Pₙ`, `Mₘ,ₙ`.
- Put aligned matrices in a fenced code block so the brackets stay lined up.
- Name operations in plain text: `span(S)`, `dim(ℝⁿ)`, `det(A)`, `rank(A)`, `Null(A)`.

Do not use `$`, `$$`, `\(...\)`, `\[...\]`, or commands such as `\mathbb`, `\mathbf`, `\operatorname`, or `\begin{bmatrix}`.

```
Bad:  $$\mathbb{R}^n=\{(x_1,\ldots,x_n):x_i\in\mathbb{R}\}$$
Good: **ℝⁿ = {(x₁, …, xₙ) : xᵢ ∈ ℝ}**
```

```
        ⎡ 1 ⎤
𝐯₁  =   ⎢ 0 ⎥
        ⎣ 1 ⎦
```

Common symbols: ℝ ∈ ⊆ ≠ ≥ ∅ × ⟹ ⟺ ↔ ← … ⋯ −. Bold vectors 𝐮 𝐯 𝐰 𝐛 𝐜 𝐱, zero vector 𝟎, subscripts ₀₁₂₃ₙₘₖᵢ, superscripts ⁰¹²³ⁿ.
